  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_bda3da3fd11045a38a1211f908d53f58",
      "statement": "BillCollector has no CI pipeline; changes are validated in the local regression test environment and in production runs before integration, and the Proof rule requires every PR to ship with a test or check (regression scenario, unit test, schema validation, or documented manual run) stating the command and expected result.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CONTRIBUTING.md#L17-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0dc5e672d3655c5361d1f8a81c151bc214a0b8352290d0dbc7f52830711bc683:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://CONTRIBUTING.md#L48-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:726df7758e7fe67e806af177100d9b92dda9b8e39dd581b83d88ab52e0691093:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L53-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:269dc3a87e721730da9da9ff36c01db684ca90fcee82ff08ce285707bba004e8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0d0b19bf0c7c40bda101550db11d5508",
      "statement": "The regression environment is a self-contained three-part setup: tests/mock_portal/ is an ASGI/uvicorn mock web portal on 127.0.0.1:8787 with sites covering the main scenarios, tests/scenarios.py holds the expected outcome of every (service, user) pair, and tests/run_regression.py starts the portal, executes every pair of a scope INI through the production scraping engine, and checks the engine return value, the DB rows, the downloaded files, and the exit semantics. It shipped in release v0.4.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CHANGELOG.md#L75-L85",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0d3b2342f95504152e4d9366a55cd8ff7de712ebe5d7c68713455b0d39626118:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L306-L312",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1d2970b4af762d0a5823184b12ac5b9caaed45231db96468a775008b086754ef:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f3415a18308749898fbdbfa8ea5a72a3",
      "statement": "The regression run is executed from the repository root with `apps/.venv/bin/python tests/run_regression.py --ini tests/bc_regression.ini` and is expected to exit 0 with all expectations matched; `--ini tests/bc_regression_happy.ini` restricts to a success-only scope, `--keep-downloads` keeps the test downloads, and `--port <n>` moves the mock portal. The same command is the verification step CONTRIBUTING.md names for changes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CONTRIBUTING.md#L64-L72",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6667e1a30e0e27c836eef17f955c401e42c4176200bb6b88738eb765840a281a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L314-L322",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2011615ceacb0c5879fd2401f1a3648e7778b94c9f9482a76bf6e0b8f67ee10d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_74ad960d3c5a41f99cc4012f9bce458b",
      "statement": "The mock portal's behavioral matrix comprises six scenarios: happy path with OTP and downloads, bad login, graceful step failure, download failure, empty document list, and CAPTCHA-style friction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CHANGELOG.md#L79-L85",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c59628c8ae3dbeb3770cef8abac52a693142a1f0f87cc986e0911103f4435ad5:"
