        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8962f66baa1e477da08fdd2e5fbf08e8",
      "statement": "The regression harness exit codes are: 0 all expectations matched, 1 at least one expectation deviated, 2 the mock portal could not be started, 3 a real BillCollector run holds the run lock, 4 the --vault preflight failed; codes 2-4 mark environment failures so only a green 0 certifies engine behavior.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L322-L322",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:255b68380a13fd9049a6735863f2eee238f7035d7f7a3f9cd7ec58d088043c0e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_200cf0a53b674694b23734c07a1d19d0",
      "statement": "The harness --vault end-to-end mode prefights a real Vaultwarden (env, DNS, unlock, sync) and fetches credentials, URL, and TOTP from the corresponding vault items instead of tests/scenarios.py; it requires a vault provisioned with the test items (the maintainer's dev setup), while the default mode is fully self-contained and needs no vault. A preflight failure exits 4.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CHANGELOG.md#L82-L85",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d784a66d2b63e79f398f49b771dd808e7db56278544dcb1a1f780330341accdb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L320-L320",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3766a52961d1b04bafa19ed4595e9e409c3c78d5615e0346ec6516203869dd79:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dd67f41dfa0d4d7695d0998cc413303b",
      "statement": "The harness drives the production batch engine path: retrieve_from_service_with_playwright validates the recipe with CheckRecipe against the schema at run start and returns True only when the run is not aborted and at least one download succeeded, while a finally block finalizes every started service run in the DB (success/failure) so the DB always holds a terminal result.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/BillCollectorServices_pw.py#L174-L194",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1910c092d6ee198603a8e8fe552f0a581a8d7f287bed6f34edbcf2d259925465:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/BillCollectorServices_pw.py#L270-L280",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3e29a5b16e12955d8f1f2eef073207a7a2073b93b16ee1d26af277f2678f11eb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3d9e6d65812245bfbd798cffae3b1a88",
      "statement": "The batch entry point isolates failures per (service, user) pair: a failed pair sets the failed flag and the loop continues with the remaining services; the process exits with code 1 if any pair failed and 0 otherwise, while vault preflight failures (pinned URL vetting, unlocked status, sync) exit 1 immediately.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/BillCollector.py#L49-L142",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:26e7c57a9ea9c5e88c1997a6b933d3512d355413e3af492531a8264e4a73b6d8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2a33b77ac2e34b639dec4a0e5625e9d3",
      "statement": "The pytest suite is configured in the repo-root pytest.ini: testpaths is tests, addopts loads -p nicegui.testing.user_plugin (the NiceGUI User fixture runs UI tests in-process without a browser; the Screen fixture's selenium dependency is not used by the committed suite), asyncio_mode is auto because the User fixture is an async fixture, and main_file points at tests/ui_test_main.py.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://pytest.ini",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:f3248148d6f1e9c143a538fcc656a69f7f40f89ddb0b98ecbbcd84b9125059b8"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7faaf0b4808a4a45b13c2ca776f821a7",
      "statement": "The daemon's filesystem paths (BC_DATA_DIR, BC_DB_DIR, BC_DB_FILE, BC_LOG_DIR, BC_BROWSER_DIR, BC_PROFILE_ROOT, BC_DOWNLOAD_DIR) are overridable via BC_* environment variables in apps/billcollector/config.py specifically to keep the test suite from touching the production apps/ data, so each test runs against a fresh temporary database.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/billcollector/config.py#L1-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fd5418a7f5c8827d8a9b7f496063cffdd7c6ef8eafb0793f7d443492857646d8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a6ff72aed7574014b3f71dadde009c18",
      "statement": "pytest, pytest-asyncio, and ruff are dev-only dependencies in apps/requirements-dev.txt that are never added to the runtime requirements.txt, so the production image never carries them; the documented suite command is `apps/.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q` from the repository root, with the lint check `apps/.venv/bin/python -m ruff check apps tests`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/requirements-dev.txt",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:c1329941a46970418ea23500a9a443d416becca49c434853a5642116a30a2f66"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e69a069d45fe44b48b334c7683c0c9a9",
      "statement": "tests/check_docker_context.py proves the .dockerignore exclusions by building a worst-case image (FROM scratch, COPY . /) from a scratch context filled with synthetic canary files - no real checkout data, no registry access - and checks that every excluded artifact stays out while every source file stays in; the expected output is `Docker context: 19 private canaries excluded, 5 source files retained`, and --dockerignore <path> allows checking a different .dockerignore as a negative control. It must be run whenever the .dockerignore, the Dockerfile, or the runtime artifacts change.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CHANGELOG.md#L58-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f82c8726fbd25abee8ec3adb9a0556d8741a01b354fe197bb21e28209bcb8a51:"
        },
        {
